# Contributor standards (package source only)

These rules apply when editing **this** blueprint package. They do **not** apply to consumer/target project harness installs.

## Skill creation gate

Before adding a new skill under `harness/skills/` (or substantially rewriting an existing package skill):

1. Read and follow `harness/skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md`.
2. Pass the Skill naming standard in [`assets-blueprint` docs/standards/skill-naming.md](https://github.com/krerapus/assets-blueprint/blob/master/docs/standards/skill-naming.md) (`<action>-<object>[-<context>]`; no roles/models/versions/redundant suffixes).
3. Use skill-creator to draft structure, description (triggering), and content.
4. Register the skill in package inventories (`package_skill_names`, `manifest.yaml`, docs) only after the skill draft meets project standards.
5. On rename: append a row to `harness/migrations/renames.log` and update all inventories.

Do not drop ad-hoc `SKILL.md` trees into `harness/skills/` without going through skill-creator.

## Commits and PRs

- Commits: follow `contributor/commands/commit.md` — conventional `type(scope): description`, **no JIRA number**.
- Pull requests: follow `contributor/commands/pr.md` — GitHub `gh`, include short **Release notes** for `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`.

## Separation from consumer harness

- Do not treat `contributor/` as content to project into consumer apps.
- Do not commit live `.cursor/` / `.claude/` trees or task-memory files into this package.
- Consumer playbooks under `harness/` and forge overlays under `blueprints/` remain for target installs only.
